{"pageProps":{"post":{"slug":"velocita-replicated-trading-on-a-raspberry-pi","title":"Velocita: A Replicated Trading System on a Raspberry Pi That Refused to Believe the Exchange","date":"2026-10-27","description":"Raft over Aeron on two NUCs and a Pi 5, 16 real swaps on Solana, a ledger that matched the chain to the billionth of a SOL, and every problem I had to solve to get there.","tags":["Distributed Systems","Raft","C++20","Aeron","Solana","Trading","Architecture"],"githubUrl":"https://github.com/vishaljha2121/Velocita","content":"\n<p>\n    On October 15, a Raspberry Pi on my desk voted to buy $12.69 of SOL. Three seconds later the trade was on the Solana blockchain. Over the next three hours, with nobody touching anything, its cluster settled <strong>16 real swaps</strong>, and every one matched the blockchain <strong>to the billionth of a SOL</strong>.\n</p>\n\n<p>\n    It lost 95 cents. The most interesting thing it did all night was refuse to believe the exchange.\n</p>\n\n<div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(170px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 2.5rem 0;\">\n    <div style=\"border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.6);\"><div style=\"font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.1;\">16 / 16</div><div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-top: 0.4rem;\">settlements equal to the chain</div></div>\n    <div style=\"border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.6);\"><div style=\"font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.1;\">126 ms</div><div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-top: 0.4rem;\">p50 commit across 3 machines</div></div>\n    <div style=\"border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.6);\"><div style=\"font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.1;\">2 s</div><div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-top: 0.4rem;\">decision to Solana block (p50)</div></div>\n    <div style=\"border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.6);\"><div style=\"font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.1;\">208 ns</div><div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-top: 0.4rem;\">kernel decision (p50)</div></div>\n    <div style=\"border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.6);\"><div style=\"font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.1;\">4–7 s</div><div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-top: 0.4rem;\">voter restarted, back in step</div></div>\n    <div style=\"border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.6);\"><div style=\"font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.1; color: #16a34a;\">0</div><div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-top: 0.4rem;\">duplicate orders or unexplained balances</div></div>\n</div>\n\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 3rem\">1. The problem</h2>\n\n<p>Real money breaks things a trading script never notices:</p>\n\n<div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;\">\n    <div style=\"border-left: 3px solid #ef4444; padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\"><strong>Crashes mid-send</strong><div style=\"color: var(--secondary); font-size: 0.95rem;\">Restart must neither lose the order nor send it twice.</div></div>\n    <div style=\"border-left: 3px solid #ef4444; padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\"><strong>An exchange you can't fully trust</strong><div style=\"color: var(--secondary); font-size: 0.95rem;\">\"Failed\" doesn't always mean \"didn't happen\".</div></div>\n    <div style=\"border-left: 3px solid #ef4444; padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\"><strong>A strategy you shouldn't trust</strong><div style=\"color: var(--secondary); font-size: 0.95rem;\">A signal bug must not be able to drain the account.</div></div>\n    <div style=\"border-left: 3px solid #ef4444; padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\"><strong>Cheap hardware</strong><div style=\"color: var(--secondary); font-size: 0.95rem;\">Two mini PCs and a Pi on home Wi-Fi.</div></div>\n</div>\n\n<p>These are the same failures that cost real trading firms money. I wanted to see if the textbook answers could hold all the way down to a $25 account on a Raspberry Pi.</p>\n\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 3rem\">2. The idea: separate deciding from doing</h2>\n\n<p>Money and decisions live in one deterministic state machine that three machines replicate with Raft. Everything that touches the outside world runs separately, acts only on committed state, and brings back evidence.</p>\n\n<div class=\"mermaid\" style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin-bottom: 2rem; background: transparent;\">\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph NUC1[\"NUC1 · x86_64\"]\n    V1[\"voter 1\"]\n    DRV[\"strategy\"]\n    GW[\"gateway\"]\n    SG[\"signer\"]\n  end\n  subgraph PI[\"Raspberry Pi 5\"]\n    V2[\"voter 2\"]\n  end\n  subgraph NUC2[\"NUC2 · x86_64\"]\n    V3[\"voter 3\"]\n  end\n  V1 <-->|\"Raft over Aeron UDP\"| V2\n  V2 <--> V3\n  V1 <--> V3\n  DRV -->|\"intent\"| V1\n  GW <-->|\"state, evidence\"| V1\n  GW <--> SG\n  GW <--> TM([\"exchange\"])\n  TM --> SOL([\"Solana\"])\n  GW -->|\"finalized reads\"| SOL\n</div>\n\n<p>One trade passes through five hands, and none can complete it alone:</p>\n\n<div class=\"mermaid\" style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin-bottom: 2rem; background: transparent;\">\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant S as Strategy\n  participant R as Raft (3 voters)\n  participant G as Gateway\n  participant K as Signer\n  participant C as Solana\n  S->>R: propose a buy\n  R->>R: commit on 2 of 3, reserve cash\n  G->>R: read the committed intent\n  G->>K: sign this exact transaction\n  K->>R: is this what was committed?\n  K-->>G: signature\n  G->>C: execute, then read it back finalized\n  G->>R: settlement with exact amounts\n</div>\n\n<table style=\"width: 100%; text-align: left; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 2rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem;\">\n    <thead>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\">\n            <th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">Decision</th>\n            <th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">Intuition</th>\n        </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>ADR 0005</strong> kernel behind Raft</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; color: var(--secondary);\">Same pure function + same log = same cents on every machine. No clocks, floats or heap.</td></tr>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>ADR 0020</strong> callers have roles</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; color: var(--secondary);\">The strategy can ask, never authorize. Even the operator can't report a fill.</td></tr>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>ADR 0021</strong> integer money</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; color: var(--secondary);\">Lamports and USDC micros. The $10 loss stop lives in replicated state.</td></tr>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>ADR 0013</strong> journal first</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; color: var(--secondary);\">Write \"about to send\" before sending, so a crash means \"maybe sent\", never \"send again\".</td></tr>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>ADR 0019</strong> one key holder</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; color: var(--secondary);\">Only the signer holds the key, and it checks the exact transaction itself.</td></tr>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>ADR 0025</strong> chain is the truth</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; color: var(--secondary);\">Money moves only on a finalized transaction matching what was signed.</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 3rem\">3. The SD card that couldn't keep up</h2>\n\n<div style=\"margin: 2rem 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\">Commit latency, p50</div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\"><div style=\"width: 9rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\">V1.1 · one Pi</div><div style=\"flex: 1; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"width: 100%; background: #ef4444; height: 22px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div><div style=\"width: 4.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;\">396 ms</div></div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem;\"><div style=\"width: 9rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\">V2 · live</div><div style=\"flex: 1; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"width: 32%; background: #22c55e; height: 22px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div><div style=\"width: 4.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;\">126 ms</div></div>\n</div>\n\n<p>Three voters on one Pi did ~9 <code>fsync</code>s per command through one SD card, and the Raft thread waited on every one. At 20 commands/s the cluster lost its leader.</p>\n\n<p>The fix: the Raft thread never touches the disk. It hands 4 KiB blocks to a writer thread over a lock-free ring.</p>\n\n<pre style=\"background: #ffffff; color: var(--foreground); border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; overflow-x: auto; font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 2rem\">bool push(const T&amp; value) noexcept {\n    const auto head = head_.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);\n    const auto tail = tail_.load(std::memory_order_acquire);\n    if (head - tail &gt;= Capacity) return false;      // full: refuse, never overwrite\n    slots_[head &amp; (Capacity - 1)] = value;\n    head_.store(head + 1, std::memory_order_release); // publish\n    return true;\n}</pre>\n\n<div style=\"margin: 2rem 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\">Raft thread time per log record, median</div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\"><div style=\"width: 9rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\">fsync on thread</div><div style=\"flex: 1; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"width: 100%; background: #ef4444; height: 22px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div><div style=\"width: 4.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;\">20.6 µs</div></div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem;\"><div style=\"width: 9rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\">writer thread</div><div style=\"flex: 1; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"width: 0.6%; min-width: 3px; background: #22c55e; height: 22px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div><div style=\"width: 4.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;\">42 ns</div></div>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: #16a34a; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-weight: 600;\">490× less</div>\n</div>\n\n<h3>…which broke Raft</h3>\n\n<p>The Raft library counts the leader's own vote as soon as an entry is appended. With async writes, that vote arrived before the entry was on disk:</p>\n\n<div class=\"mermaid\" style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin-bottom: 2rem; background: transparent;\">\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant L as Leader\n  participant F1 as Follower 1\n  participant F2 as Follower 2\n  L->>F1: entry 42 (leader's copy only in memory)\n  F1-->>L: durable\n  Note over L: majority, commit 42\n  Note over L: crash, restart without 42\n  Note over F1: briefly unreachable\n  L->>F2: elect a leader: neither has 42\n  Note over L,F2: committed entry 42 is gone\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"border-left: 3px solid var(--foreground); padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem; margin: 2rem 0; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.03);\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 0.25rem;\">ADR 0006 · the fix</div>\n    <div>A pinned fork adds a <code>durable_idx</code> hook: the leader's vote counts only up to what is really on disk. The build refuses to compile without the patch.</div>\n</div>\n\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 3rem\">4. Memory that never grows</h2>\n\n<p>Nothing on the Raft path asks the OS for memory after start-up. Every object has a size fixed at compile time, and \"full\" is a typed refusal, never a slowdown or an out-of-memory kill.</p>\n\n<div style=\"margin: 2rem 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;\">Size budgets, enforced by <code>static_assert</code>: green under 90%, amber 90–99%, dark exactly at budget (deliberate: one cache line, the swap account sized to fit)</div>\n    <div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.6rem;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\"><span>whole replicated state</span><span style=\"font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap;\">78,512 / 81,920 B</span></div><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.06); border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 0.2rem;\"><div style=\"width: 95.8%; background: #f59e0b; height: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.6rem;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\"><span>canonical snapshot</span><span style=\"font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap;\">61,586 / 65,536 B</span></div><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.06); border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 0.2rem;\"><div style=\"width: 94.0%; background: #f59e0b; height: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.6rem;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\"><span>swap account</span><span style=\"font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap;\">4,160 / 4,160 B</span></div><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.06); border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 0.2rem;\"><div style=\"width: 100.0%; background: var(--foreground); height: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.6rem;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\"><span>kernel result</span><span style=\"font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap;\">112 / 128 B</span></div><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.06); border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 0.2rem;\"><div style=\"width: 87.5%; background: #22c55e; height: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.6rem;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\"><span>swap command</span><span style=\"font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap;\">296 / 512 B</span></div><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.06); border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 0.2rem;\"><div style=\"width: 57.8%; background: #22c55e; height: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 0.6rem;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\"><span>hot record (one cache line)</span><span style=\"font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap;\">64 / 64 B</span></div><div style=\"background: rgba(0,0,0,0.06); border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 0.2rem;\"><div style=\"width: 100.0%; background: var(--foreground); height: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div></div>\n</div>\n\n<pre style=\"background: #ffffff; color: var(--foreground); border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; overflow-x: auto; font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 2rem\">static_assert(std::is_trivially_copyable_v&lt;State&gt;);\nstatic_assert(sizeof(State)   &lt;= 4160);   // add a field, the build fails\nstatic_assert(sizeof(Command) &lt;= 512);</pre>\n\n<div style=\"margin: 2rem 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;\">The memory atlas: where the 80 KiB state budget goes</div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; height: 30px; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;\"><div title=\"request receipts: 40,960 B\" style=\"width: 50.00%; background: #6366f1; \"></div><div title=\"decision records: 10,368 B\" style=\"width: 12.66%; background: #8b5cf6; \"></div><div title=\"policies: 7,360 B\" style=\"width: 8.98%; background: #0ea5e9; \"></div><div title=\"source receipts: 7,168 B\" style=\"width: 8.75%; background: #14b8a6; \"></div><div title=\"policy bundles: 4,176 B\" style=\"width: 5.10%; background: #22c55e; \"></div><div title=\"swap account: 4,160 B\" style=\"width: 5.08%; background: #f59e0b; \"></div><div title=\"risk, orders, cursors: 4,320 B\" style=\"width: 5.27%; background: #94a3b8; \"></div><div title=\"free: 3,408 B\" style=\"width: 4.16%; background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border);\"></div></div>\n    <div style=\"margin-top: 0.6rem; line-height: 1.8;\"><span style=\"display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; margin-right: 1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--secondary);\"><span style=\"width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; background: #6366f1;  display: inline-block;\"></span>request receipts 40.0 KiB</span><span style=\"display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; margin-right: 1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--secondary);\"><span style=\"width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; background: #8b5cf6;  display: inline-block;\"></span>decision records 10.1 KiB</span><span style=\"display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; margin-right: 1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--secondary);\"><span style=\"width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; background: #0ea5e9;  display: inline-block;\"></span>policies 7.2 KiB</span><span style=\"display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; margin-right: 1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--secondary);\"><span style=\"width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; background: #14b8a6;  display: inline-block;\"></span>source receipts 7.0 KiB</span><span style=\"display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; margin-right: 1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--secondary);\"><span style=\"width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;  display: inline-block;\"></span>policy bundles 4.1 KiB</span><span style=\"display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; margin-right: 1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--secondary);\"><span style=\"width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; background: #f59e0b;  display: inline-block;\"></span>swap account 4.1 KiB</span><span style=\"display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; margin-right: 1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--secondary);\"><span style=\"width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; background: #94a3b8;  display: inline-block;\"></span>risk, orders, cursors 4.2 KiB</span><span style=\"display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; margin-right: 1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--secondary);\"><span style=\"width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--secondary); display: inline-block;\"></span>free 3.3 KiB</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<p>Half the state is receipts: the stored answer to each recent command, so a retry gets the original answer instead of a second trade.</p>\n\n<table style=\"width: 100%; text-align: left; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 2rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem;\">\n    <thead>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">Arena</th><th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">Slots</th><th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; text-align: right;\">Total</th><th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0 0.75rem 1rem;\">When full</th></tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">retained Raft log</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">8,192 × 2 KiB ring</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; text-align: right;\">16 MiB</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0 0.75rem 1rem; color: var(--secondary);\">refuse until compaction (64 cells kept for \"halt\")</td></tr>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">WAL blocks</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">64 × 4 KiB</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; text-align: right;\">256 KiB</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0 0.75rem 1rem; color: var(--secondary);\">backpressure</td></tr>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">result ledger</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">1,024 answers</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; text-align: right;\">–</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0 0.75rem 1rem; color: var(--secondary);\">refuse new commands, never drop an answer</td></tr>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">state tables</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">fixed arrays + count</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; text-align: right;\">77 KiB</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0 0.75rem 1rem; color: var(--secondary);\">typed \"capacity exceeded\"</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<div style=\"margin: 2rem 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;\">The 64 WAL blocks at one illustrative moment: the Raft thread fills, the writer thread syncs</div>\n    <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(16, 1fr); gap: 3px; max-width: 520px;\"><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #22c55e;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #f59e0b;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #f59e0b;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #f59e0b;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #f59e0b;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #f59e0b;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: #6366f1;\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div><div style=\"aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\"></div></div>\n    <div style=\"margin-top: 0.6rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--secondary);\"><span style=\"color: #22c55e;\">■</span> durable, reusable &nbsp; <span style=\"color: #f59e0b;\">■</span> sealed, waiting for fsync &nbsp; <span style=\"color: #6366f1;\">■</span> open, being filled &nbsp; ■ never used</div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"border-left: 3px solid var(--foreground); padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem; margin: 2rem 0; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.03);\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 0.25rem;\">ADR 0022 · budgets are compile errors</div>\n    <div>The snapshot must fit one 64 KiB message. As a runtime check, growing a struct would surface in production as a snapshot that no longer fits; as a <code>static_assert</code>, the build fails on both CPUs and whoever adds the field decides what to give up.</div>\n</div>\n\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 3rem\">5. Elections nobody asked for</h2>\n\n<div style=\"margin: 2rem 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\">Compaction pause (election timeout is 1–2 s)</div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\"><div style=\"width: 9rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\">re-read everything</div><div style=\"flex: 1; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"width: 100%; background: #ef4444; height: 22px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div><div style=\"width: 4.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;\">4.8 s</div></div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem;\"><div style=\"width: 9rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\">rotating scrub</div><div style=\"flex: 1; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"width: 8%; background: #22c55e; height: 22px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div><div style=\"width: 4.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;\">≤ 0.4 s</div></div>\n</div>\n\n<table style=\"width: 100%; text-align: left; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 2rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem;\">\n    <thead>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">Symptom</th><th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">Cause</th><th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">Fix</th></tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0; color: #ef4444;\"><strong>term 1 → 65</strong> in 48 h</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0;\">every compaction re-read all archives</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">check 2 segments per compaction, in rotation</td></tr>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0; color: #ef4444;\"><strong>term 49 → 191</strong> in 6 h</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0;\">a voter back from a Wi-Fi drop deposed the leader</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">pre-vote: ask before campaigning</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 3rem\">6. The gateway that stopped itself, twice</h2>\n\n<p>The gateway stops when anything looks off, because a stop might hide an order in flight. That paranoia surfaced two bugs:</p>\n\n<table style=\"width: 100%; text-align: left; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 2rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem;\">\n    <thead>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">When</th><th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">What happened</th><th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">Fix</th></tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0; vertical-align: top;\">Oct 9, paper</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0;\">Heard \"filled\" from a follower, then read older state from a slower leader (the Pi)</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">read fence: discard any state older than what you've seen</td></tr>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0; vertical-align: top;\">Oct 15, pre-live</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 0;\">One failed read during an election stopped it for good</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">retry reads for 120 s; failed <em>commands</em> still stop</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 3rem\">7. One process holds the key, and trusts no one</h2>\n\n<p>The gateway talks to the internet, so it never sees the key. The signer re-checks everything itself before signing:</p>\n\n<div class=\"mermaid\" style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin-bottom: 2rem; background: transparent;\">\nflowchart LR\n  A[\"sign request\"] --> B[\"re-read Raft:<br/>effect prepared?\"]\n  B --> C[\"decode the transaction:<br/>amounts, fee, DEX match?\"]\n  C --> D[\"authority proof<br/>from Raft\"]\n  D --> E[\"journal, then sign\"]\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"border-left: 3px solid var(--foreground); padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem; margin: 2rem 0; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.03);\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 0.25rem;\">ADR 0019 · decode, don't simulate</div>\n    <div>A simulation shows what a transaction would do <em>now</em>. Decoding proves what the signature <em>allows</em>: which accounts, how much at most, and the minimum that must arrive.</div>\n</div>\n\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 3rem\">8. 16 out of 16, to the atom</h2>\n\n<p>Every amount in Velocita is an integer count of an asset's smallest unit, called an <strong>atom</strong>:</p>\n\n<div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;\">\n    <div style=\"border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.6);\"><div style=\"font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--secondary);\">SOL · base</div><div style=\"font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0.3rem;\">1 SOL = 1,000,000,000 lamports</div><div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-top: 0.3rem;\"><code>BaseAtoms</code></div></div>\n    <div style=\"border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.6);\"><div style=\"font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--secondary);\">USDC · quote</div><div style=\"font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0.3rem;\">1 USDC = 1,000,000 micros</div><div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-top: 0.3rem;\"><code>QuoteAtoms</code></div></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 0 0 2rem;\">\n    <div style=\"border-left: 3px solid #22c55e; padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\"><strong>Same bits everywhere</strong><div style=\"color: var(--secondary); font-size: 0.95rem;\">Floats round differently on Intel and ARM; integers can't fork the replicas.</div></div>\n    <div style=\"border-left: 3px solid #22c55e; padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\"><strong>Equal to the chain</strong><div style=\"color: var(--secondary); font-size: 0.95rem;\">Solana stores balances in these units, so a settlement compares with <code>==</code>, no tolerance.</div></div>\n    <div style=\"border-left: 3px solid #22c55e; padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\"><strong>Can't be mixed up</strong><div style=\"color: var(--secondary); font-size: 0.95rem;\">Two distinct types: adding lamports to USDC doesn't compile.</div></div>\n</div>\n\n<pre style=\"background: #ffffff; color: var(--foreground); border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; overflow-x: auto; font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 2rem\">using BaseAtoms  = StrongId&lt;BaseAtomTag&gt;;    // lamports\nusing QuoteAtoms = StrongId&lt;QuoteAtomTag&gt;;   // USDC micros</pre>\n\n<p>One buy, followed through the system in atoms:</p>\n\n<div class=\"mermaid\" style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin-bottom: 2rem; background: transparent;\">\nflowchart LR\n  D[\"strategy<br/>debit 12,690,000<br/>min 110,400,000 lamports\"] --> K[\"kernel<br/>reserves 12,690,000\"]\n  K --> S[\"signer<br/>fee = 12,690,000 ÷ 10,000 × 20<br/>= 25,380 exactly\"]\n  S --> C[\"Solana<br/>+119,507,269 lamports<br/>−12,690,000 micros\"]\n  C --> T[\"settlement<br/>same integers\"]\n  T --> UI[\"dashboard<br/>$ only for display\"]\n</div>\n\n<p>That division is why every buy is a whole number of cents: the signer refuses an input that isn't a multiple of 10,000 atoms, so the fee always comes out exact. And the books and the chain end up holding the same integers:</p>\n\n<table style=\"width: 100%; text-align: left; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 2rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem;\">\n    <thead>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">Effect 1 (buy)</th><th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; text-align: right;\">In Raft</th><th style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; text-align: right;\">On chain</th></tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">SOL (lamports)</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; text-align: right;\">119,507,269</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; text-align: right; color: #22c55e;\">+119,507,269</td></tr>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\"><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0;\">USDC (micros)</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; text-align: right;\">12,690,000</td><td style=\"padding: 0.75rem 0; text-align: right; color: #22c55e;\">−12,690,000</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 3rem\">9. Effect 25: the exchange said \"failed\"</h2>\n\n<div class=\"mermaid\" style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin-bottom: 2rem; background: transparent;\">\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant G as Gateway\n  participant T as Exchange\n  participant C as Solana\n  G->>T: execute buy (effect 25)\n  T->>C: submit\n  Note over C: lands in slot 457,481,187 and fails\n  T-->>G: failed, executed 0, NO transaction hash\n  Note over G: nothing to verify, so hold the $12.69\n  Note over G: stop after 3 min\n  Note over G,C: new on-chain proof built for \"never executed\"\n  Note over G: proof refuses\n</div>\n\n<p>Believing the exchange would have recorded a transaction that <em>did</em> reach the chain as one that never did. Had it succeeded late, the same cash could have been spent twice. I later found it in the wallet's history: it landed in the same second the order was created, failed inside a DEX, and moved none of our money.</p>\n\n<div style=\"border-left: 3px solid var(--foreground); padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem; margin: 2rem 0; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.03);\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 0.25rem;\">ADR 0027 · unknown is a state</div>\n    <div>\"We don't know\" keeps the money reserved. Once a signature might exist, only the chain can close it.</div>\n</div>\n\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 3rem\">10. Pull the plug on the Pi</h2>\n\n<div class=\"mermaid\" style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin-bottom: 2rem; background: transparent;\">\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant N1 as NUC1 (leader)\n  participant N2 as NUC2\n  participant P as Pi\n  Note over P: offline\n  N1->>N2: new entries\n  N2-->>N1: durable: 2 of 3, keep going\n  Note over P: restarts, replays its own log\n  N1->>P: the entries it missed\n  Note over N1,P: 3 of 3, identical state\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin: 2rem 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\">Stop to back in step, rolling upgrade on Oct 16</div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\"><div style=\"width: 9rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\">Raspberry Pi</div><div style=\"flex: 1; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"width: 100%; background: #22c55e; height: 22px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div><div style=\"width: 4.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;\">7 s</div></div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\"><div style=\"width: 9rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\">NUC2</div><div style=\"flex: 1; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"width: 57%; background: #22c55e; height: 22px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div><div style=\"width: 4.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;\">4 s</div></div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem;\"><div style=\"width: 9rem; font-size: 0.85rem;\">NUC1 (leader)</div><div style=\"flex: 1; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"width: 57%; background: #22c55e; height: 22px; border-radius: 4px;\"></div></div><div style=\"width: 4.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;\">4 s</div></div>\n</div>\n\n<p>Earlier, during an upgrade, the Pi was down for minutes; the NUCs kept committing and the Pi caught up from its own log when it returned.</p>\n\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 3rem\">11. Where the 95 cents went</h2>\n\n<div style=\"margin: 2rem 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\">Cost of one round trip, ~94 bp</div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; height: 34px; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; font-size: 0.8rem; color: #fff; font-weight: 600;\">\n        <div style=\"width: 42.5%; background: #f59e0b; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\">fees 40 bp</div>\n        <div style=\"width: 55.3%; background: #ef4444; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\">exchange price 52 bp</div>\n        <div style=\"width: 2.2%; background: #64748b;\"></div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--secondary); margin-top: 0.5rem;\">The market itself moved only −2 bp (grey) between buy and sell.</div>\n</div>\n\n<p>The strategy was a test load with no edge, and replays had said so. The live run measured the cost: a one-second strategy here needs a ~1% move just to break even. The system worked; the economics never could.</p>\n\n<h2 style=\"margin-top: 3rem\">What I took away</h2>\n\n<ul>\n    <li><strong>Measure first.</strong> Every fix above started as a number that looked wrong.</li>\n    <li><strong>Fixes create bugs.</strong> The 490× speedup quietly broke Raft; only a test of every crash point caught it.</li>\n    <li><strong>Refusing is a feature.</strong> The best thing it did with real money was say \"I can't prove that\".</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>\n    Code, 29 decision records and every number here: <a href=\"https://github.com/vishaljha2121/Velocita\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GitHub</a> · <a href=\"https://github.com/vishaljha2121/Velocita/blob/main/RESULTS.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">results</a> · <a href=\"https://github.com/vishaljha2121/Velocita/tree/main/docs/guide\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">guide</a>. Built with Claude and Codex as coding collaborators, directed and reviewed by me.\n</p>\n        "}},"__N_SSG":true}